{"uid":"modules/loop_progress.py","name":"loop_progress.py","qualname":"modules/loop_progress.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/loop_progress.py","line":1,"end_line":368,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Rich Live milestone panel for the autonomous loop.","description":"Renders the orchestrator chain as persistent milestones — green done,\nblue in-progress (spinner), red still pending — plus intent/fact/finding\ncounts, elapsed time and the latest activity line. The panel stays on\nscreen when the run finishes.\n\nRobustness rules (learned the hard way):\n\n- No markup strings anywhere: every cell is a ``Text`` object with an\n  explicit style, so literal ``[green]`` tags can never leak and foreign\n  ``[brackets]`` in activity lines can never crash rendering.\n- Fixed panel width (100 cols) with non-wrapping cells: narrow sinks\n  cannot corrupt the live region by wrapping.\n- Non-terminal sinks never use ``Live`` (Rich would degrade to printing\n  every refresh as a full new panel): they get one compact milestone\n  line per stage change plus the final table at stop.\n- All output goes through :mod:`core.safe_console`: no ANSI codes on\n  non-tty sinks, ASCII box and markers when stdout cannot encode UTF-8.\n- Stage states are inferred from the task overview, never asserted.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/loop_progress.py::CHAIN_STAGES","modules/loop_progress.py::LoopSnapshot","modules/loop_progress.py::snapshot_from_overview","modules/loop_progress.py::snap_to_states","modules/loop_progress.py::sanitize_line","modules/loop_progress.py::LoopProgress"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
